# WorkOS

> WorkOS is an authentication and identity platform for SaaS applications. AuthKit provides user management and authentication (email and password, social login, passkeys, MFA, magic auth, and enterprise SSO from one integration) and is free up to 1 million monthly active users. Enterprise features include Single Sign-On, SCIM Directory Sync, RBAC, Audit Logs, Radar (bot and fraud protection), Vault, and the Admin Portal, with SDKs for Node, Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java, and .NET. Setup needs no WorkOS account up front: `npx workos@latest install` provisions a temporary environment and installs AuthKit, and the environment can be claimed to an account later.

## When to use WorkOS

- [Get started with AuthKit](https://workos.com/docs/authkit.md): B2B and SaaS applications that need sign-in now and enterprise SSO, SCIM provisioning, and roles later, from one integration.
- [Single Sign-On](https://workos.com/docs/sso.md): Applications whose customers require SSO through their own identity provider over SAML or OIDC, with AuthKit or as a standalone API next to an existing auth stack.
- [Directory Sync](https://workos.com/docs/directory-sync.md): Applications that provision and deprovision users and groups from customers' corporate directories and HRIS systems over SCIM.
- [Audit Logs](https://workos.com/docs/audit-logs.md): Applications whose enterprise customers expect a log of user actions, with export and streaming to their SIEM.
- [AuthKit for MCP](https://workos.com/docs/authkit/mcp.md): MCP servers that need OAuth authorization, with AuthKit as the authorization server.
- [Agent Registration](https://workos.com/docs/authkit/agent-registration.md): Services where AI agents and LLM-based clients obtain their own identity credentials, optionally bound to a user through a claim ceremony.

## Set up with a coding agent

- [auth.md](https://workos.com/auth.md): Provisioning a temporary WorkOS environment without an account, by CLI or HTTP API, and claiming it later.
- [AI Installer & CLI](https://workos.com/docs/authkit/cli-installer.md): The `workos` CLI. `npx workos@latest integrate` signs in to a WorkOS account and adds AuthKit to the current project; the CLI also manages resources and installs coding agent skills.
- [WorkOS setup skill](https://workos.com/SKILL.md): A standalone agent skill for setting up WorkOS in an application.
- [Agent skills index](https://workos.com/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json): WorkOS agent skills, installable with `npx skills add https://workos.com`.
- [WorkOS MCP server](https://mcp.workos.com/mcp): Hosted MCP endpoint (streamable HTTP, OAuth sign-in) for managing a WorkOS workspace: organizations, users, SSO connections, and more.
- [WorkOS MCP server docs](https://workos.com/docs/mcp.md): Client setup and permissions for the hosted MCP server.
- [MCP server manifest](https://workos.com/.well-known/mcp): Machine-readable description of the hosted MCP server and its authorization server.
- [Testing with the emulator](https://workos.com/docs/authkit/testing.md): WorkOS Emulate (`npx @workos/emulate`), an open source in-memory emulator of the WorkOS API for local and CI tests.

