## Products

- [AuthKit](https://workos.com/authkit): User management and authentication: email and password, social login, passkeys, MFA, magic auth, and enterprise SSO.
- [Single Sign-On](https://workos.com/single-sign-on): Enterprise SSO over SAML and OIDC with identity providers through one API.
- [Directory Sync](https://workos.com/directory-sync): SCIM user and group provisioning from directory providers such as Okta and Microsoft Entra ID.
- [Admin Portal](https://workos.com/admin-portal): Hosted UI where customers' IT admins verify domains and configure SSO and Directory Sync connections.
- [Audit Logs](https://workos.com/audit-logs): Event logs of user actions, with export and streaming to SIEM providers.
- [Role-Based Access Control](https://workos.com/rbac): Roles and permissions, including organization-scoped roles and role assignment from identity provider groups.
- [Radar](https://workos.com/radar): Real-time detection and blocking of bots, account abuse, and credential theft.
- [Vault](https://workos.com/vault): Enterprise key management and encrypted storage for tokens, passwords, certificates, files, and other customer data.
- [Multi-Factor Authentication](https://workos.com/multi-factor-authentication): Second factors such as authenticator apps and SMS through one API.
- [Secure auth for MCP servers](https://workos.com/mcp): OAuth 2.1 authorization for MCP servers, with scopes and tool permissions.
- [Pipes](https://workos.com/pipes): Connections to users' third-party accounts such as GitHub, Slack, Google, and Salesforce, with OAuth, credential storage, and token refresh handled by WorkOS.

## Pricing

- [Pricing](https://workos.com/pricing.md): AuthKit is free up to 1 million monthly active users; Single Sign-On and Directory Sync are priced per connection with volume discounts; Audit Logs, Radar, custom domains, and support plans are priced separately; staging environments are free.
